      { question: "How does a VFD compressor keep pipeline pressure stable?", answer: "A VFD works within a tight pressure window of roughly ±0.1 bar, adjusting motor RPM by fractions to hold a flat pressure line, whereas fixed-speed units oscillate across a 1.0 to 1.5 bar band. This stable pressure protects sensitive pneumatic calibration equipment, ensures consistent laser cutting finishes, and optimizes automated assembly lines." }
